  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contributing to Addressing Housing Needs of Displaced Populations from Donetsk Oblast</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Two years following Russia&#x2019;s invasion of Ukraine, 3.7 million people remain internally displaced (IDPs). Thousands of people have been forced to shelter in collective IDP centers or damaged buildings. In response to this, IOM is currently implementing an initiative to provide transitional housing solutions for the most vulnerable among displaced people from Mariupol by renovating former student dormitories in Dnipro city to become habitational units.</narrative>
  </description>
